ion-type="journal">Chong, J.P., P. Th&#x000f6;mmes, A. Rowles, H.M. Mahbubani, and J.J. Blow. <year>1997</year>. Characterization of the <italic>Xenopus</italic> replication licensing system. <source>Methods Enzymol.</source> <volume>283</volume>:<fpage>549</fpage>&#x02013;564.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9251047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Cortez, D., G. Glick, and S.J. Elledge. <year>2004</year>. Minichromosome maintenance proteins are direct targets of the ATM and ATR checkpoint kinases. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>101</volume>:<fpage>10078</fpage>&#x02013;10083.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15210935</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Danis, E., K. Brodolin, S. Menut, D. Maiorano, C. Girard-Reydet, and M. Mechali. <year>2004</year>. Specification of a DNA replication origin by a transcription complex. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>721</fpage>&#x02013;730.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15247921</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">DePamphilis, M.L. <year>1999</year>. Replication origins in metazoan chromosomes: fact or fiction? <source>Bioessays.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>5</fpage>&#x02013;16.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10070250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Diffley, J.F. <year>2004</year>. Regulation of early events in chromosome replication. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>R778</fpage>&#x02013;R786.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15380092</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Dimitrova, D.S., I.T. Todorov, T. Melendy, and D.M. Gilbert. <year>1999</year>. Mcm2, but not RPA, is a component of the mammalian early G1-phase prereplication complex. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>146</volume>:<fpage>709</fpage>&#x02013;722.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10459007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Dimitrova, D.S., T.A. Prokhorova, J.J. Blow, I.T. Todorov, and D.M. Gilbert. <year>2002</year>. Mammalian nuclei become licensed for DNA replication during late telophase. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>115</volume>:<fpage>51</fpage>&#x02013;59.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11801723</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Donovan, S., J. Harwood, L.S. Drury, and J.F. Diffley. <year>1997</year>. Cdc6p-dependent loading of Mcm proteins onto pre-replicative chromatin in budding yeast. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>94</volume>:<fpage>5611</fpage>&#x02013;5616.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9159120</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Edwards, M.C., A.V. Tutter, C. Cvetic, C.H. Gilbert, T.A. Prokhorova, and J.C. Walter. <year>2002</year>. MCM2-7 complexes bind chromatin in a distributed pattern surrounding the origin recognition complex in <italic>Xenopus</italic> egg extracts. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>277</volume>:<fpage>33049</fpage>&#x02013;33057.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12087101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Fraser, A.G., R.S. Kamath, P. Zipperlen, M. Martinez-Campos, M. Sohrmann, and J. Ahringer. <year>2000</year>. Functional genomic analysis of <italic>C. elegans</italic> chromosome I by systematic RNA interference. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>408</volume>:<fpage>325</fpage>&#x02013;330.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11099033</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Gilbert, D.M. <year>2001</year>. Making sense of eukaryotic DNA replication origins. <source>Science.</source> <volume>294</volume>:<fpage>96</fpage>&#x02013;100.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11588251</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Gillespie, P.J., A. Li, and J.J. Blow. <year>2001</year>. Reconstitution of licensed replication origins on <italic>Xenopus</italic> sperm nuclei using purified proteins. <source>BMC Biochem.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>15</fpage>.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11737877</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Griffiths, T.D., and S.Y. Ling. <year>1985</year>. Effect of ultraviolet light on thymidine incorporation, DNA chain elongation and replicon initiation in wild-type and excision-deficient Chinese hamster ovary cells. <source>Biochim. Biophys. Acta.</source> <volume>826</volume>:<fpage>121</fpage>&#x02013;128.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4052429</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Griffiths, T.D., and S.Y. Ling. <year>1987</year>. Activation of alternative sites of replicon initiation in Chinese hamster cells exposed to ultraviolet light. <source>Mutat. Res.</source> <volume>184</volume>:<fpage>39</fpage>&#x02013;46.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3600681</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Griffiths, T.D., and S.Y. Ling. <year>1989</year>. Effects of UV light on DNA chain growth and replicon initiation in human cells. <source>Mutat. Res.</source> <volume>218</volume>:<fpage>87</fpage>&#x02013;94.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2770767</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Harvey, K.J., and J. Newport. <year>2003</year>. CpG methylation of DNA restricts prereplication complex assembly in <italic>Xenopus</italic> egg extracts. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>23</volume>:<fpage>6769</fpage>&#x02013;6779.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12972597</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Hekmat-Nejad, M., Z. You, M.C. Yee, J.W. Newport, and K.A. Cimprich. <year>2000</year>. <italic>Xenopus</italic> ATR is a replication-dependent chromatin-binding protein required for the DNA replication checkpoint. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>1565</fpage>&#x02013;1573.<pub-id